# Force LF line endings for scripts that must run correctly on Linux/WSL,
# regardless of the cloning machine's core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# a Windows checkout can silently reintroduce CRLF into bootstrap/setup.sh,
# which breaks bash outright ("syntax error near unexpected token").
*.sh text eol=lf

# Let git decide sensibly for everything else, rather than leaving line
# endings entirely up to each contributor's local autocrlf setting.
* text=auto
